# T2 harness change discipline

When editing the T0/T1/T2 harness (these globs), the contract is duplicated in
docs and guidance. A behavior change here MUST update, in the same change:

- `scripts/tests/test-minikube-t2-contract.sh` and
  `scripts/tests/test-minikube-t2-scenarios.sh` (they assert harness behavior)
- `docs/testing/minikube-t2-runbook.md`
- `.cursor/rules/minikube-t0-t1-t2.mdc` and
  `.cursor/skills/minikube-t0-t1-t2/` (SKILL.md + reference.md)
- the T0/T1/T2 sections of `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`

Invariants that must never regress:

- Final T2 verdict = `t2.sh run_final_preflight` with `T2_PLAN_MODE=false`
  and plan state `already-synced`; anything else is `HEAD_MARKER_MISMATCH`.
- Planner mode `T2_PLAN_MODE=true` exists only inside the orchestrator so
  `full-bootstrap` is reachable; standalone preflight stays fail-loud.
- T1 stays fail-loud (no green on unavailable DSN or zero tests); role-reset
  suites keep the throwaway Postgres 16.
- `t2.sh` keeps `IMAGE_SOURCE=local` for bootstrap/reconcile and calls
  `pre-gate-sync` with `--skip-port-forwards`.
- `t2_process_check` accepts only real `kubectl` (`comm=kubectl`) port-forward
  PIDs recorded in the profile cache or legacy `/tmp/pf-<profile>-*.pid`.
  awk is a loose pre-filter: `kubectl` as argv0/path token and a later
  standalone `port-forward` token (flags may sit between them).
- Stable failure codes (`BOOTSTRAP_REQUIRED`, `HEAD_MARKER_MISMATCH`,
  `PORT_FORWARD_CONFLICT`, `PROFILE_BUSY`, ...) keep their meanings.

Run T0 locally before proposing harness changes:

```bash
bash scripts/tests/test-minikube-t2-contract.sh
bash scripts/tests/test-minikube-t2-scenarios.sh
```
